-america-as-a-garden-plant-scientists-now-warn-its-tangled-vines-can-become-wildfire-fuel/articleshow/133679773.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/kudzu-was-brought-to-america-as-a-garden-plant-scientists-now-warn-its-tangled-vines-can-become-wildfire-fuel/articleshow/133679773.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-01T17:13:22+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133679941,imgsize-2321595.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Arkansas tried to blow up a 93-year-old bridge, but it survived the blast in 2016]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133678113.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[An Arkansas bridge demolition failed unexpectedly on October 11, 2016. Explosives weakened the structure, but it did not collapse as planned. Crews then used barges and cables to bring down the aged structure. A new bridge was constructed and opened to traffic in March 2017. The unusual demolition became a memorable part of the bridge's history.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2016-arkansas-tried-to-blow-up-a-93-year-old-bridge-to-begin-a-98-4-million-replacement-the-explosives-went-off-and-the-bridge-simply-wobbled-back-into-place/articleshow/133678113.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2016-arkansas-tried-to-blow-up-a-93-year-old-bridge-to-begin-a-98-4-million-replacement-the-explosives-went-off-and-the-bridge-simply-wobbled-back-into-place/articleshow/133678113.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-01T17:12:50+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133678345,imgsize-527368.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[UK researchers made a reef from 50 tonnes of coal waste; marine life arrived within 3 weeks]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133679315.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Researchers created an artificial reef from coal-fired power station waste in Poole Bay. Marine life began colonizing the structure almost immediately after its deployment. Adult lobsters and edible crabs reached the reef within three weeks of its placement. The structure attracted schools of pouting and supported reproduction for several species. This experiment showed industrial waste could become a productive marine habitat.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/in-1989-uk-researchers-turned-50-tonnes-of-coal-fired-power-station-waste-into-an-underwater-reef-lobsters-and-crabs-arrived-within-3-weeks/articleshow/133679315.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/in-1989-uk-researchers-turned-50-tonnes-of-coal-fired-power-station-waste-into-an-underwater-reef-lobsters-and-crabs-arrived-within-3-weeks/articleshow/133679315.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-01T17:12:46+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133679523,imgsize-1192060.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[17-year-old girl who recorded California mosque shooting livestream charged with murder]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133679901.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/17-year-old-girl-who-recorded-california-mosque-shooting-livestream-charged-with-murder/articleshow/133679901.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/17-year-old-girl-who-recorded-california-mosque-shooting-livestream-charged-with-murder/articleshow/133679901.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-01T17:10:56+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133680112,imgsize-100876.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[20 years ago, Dawn Robinson paid $40,000 for 2.4 acres in New Jersey; Middle Township is now trying to take the land for just $7,000 more]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133675854.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A woman from South Jersey has taken a stand against the government's plan to acquire her land, which is intended for a new housing development in Middle Township. She asserts that the seizure does not serve public interest. Ongoing legal proceedings and negotiations haven't resolved the matter, underscoring the potential consequences of eminent domain on marginalized communities.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/about-20-years-ago-dawn-robinson-paid-40000-for-2-4-acres-in-new-jersey-middle-township-later-offered-her-47000-and-is-now-trying-to-take-the-land-for-a-340-home-project/articleshow/133675854.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/about-20-years-ago-dawn-robinson-paid-40000-for-2-4-acres-in-new-jersey-middle-township-later-offered-her-47000-and-is-now-trying-to-take-the-land-for-a-340-home-project/articleshow/133675854.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-01T16:30:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133675979,imgsize-2240459.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Times Square stabbing: Who is Pamela Cisneros? Attacker had mental health history]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10"