nk><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-four-month-old-baby-was-buried-without-a-marker-in-1906-120-years-later-her-cemetery-finally-gave-her-a-headstone/articleshow/133674172.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-four-month-old-baby-was-buried-without-a-marker-in-1906-120-years-later-her-cemetery-finally-gave-her-a-headstone/articleshow/133674172.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-01T17:20:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133674172,imgsize-319024.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[In 1965, Bob Hope bought a 212-acre former Hollywood movie ranch which is now a public park]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133673758.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1965-bob-hope-bought-a-212-acre-former-hollywood-movie-ranch-after-thousands-of-westerns-were-filmed-there-plans-emerged-to-turn-much-of-it-into-a-park/articleshow/133673758.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1965-bob-hope-bought-a-212-acre-former-hollywood-movie-ranch-after-thousands-of-westerns-were-filmed-there-plans-emerged-to-turn-much-of-it-into-a-park/articleshow/133673758.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-01T14:40:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133673758,imgsize-322927.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[12,000-year-old skeletons in Italy reveal a mother-daughter relationship]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133677103.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Archaeologists discovered two skeletons in an embrace within Romito Cave over twelve thousand years ago. Genetic analysis revealed these individuals were both female and closely related, likely mother and daughter. The younger skeleton showed a rare inherited disorder affecting growth and limb development. This finding confirms the existence of genetic diseases in ancient human populations. The discovery also suggests prehistoric communities provided care for individuals with physical limitations.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/12000-year-old-skeletons-buried-in-an-embrace-in-italy-were-women-with-ancient-dna-revealing-a-mother-daughter-link-and-rare-genetic-disease/articleshow/133677103.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/12000-year-old-skeletons-buried-in-an-embrace-in-italy-were-women-with-ancient-dna-revealing-a-mother-daughter-link-and-rare-genetic-disease/articleshow/133677103.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-01T17:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133677327,imgsize-94288.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Scientists acidified an Ontario lake for 17 years; decades later, trout remain below half their former level]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133676293.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A groundbreaking 17-year study on Lake 223 in Ontario revealed a complex response to acid rain. While the water chemistry has recovered since the experiment ended, the ecosystem is lagging behind. Fish numbers have not rebounded as hoped, with growth rates remaining low. This underscores the vital message that true ecological healing involves much more than merely restoring chemical balance.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/scientists-added-sulfuric-acid-weekly-to-an-ontario-lake-for-17-years-lowering-ph-from-6-8-to-5-2-decades-later-its-lake-trout-population-remains-below-half-its-former-level/articleshow/133676293.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/scientists-added-sulfuric-acid-weekly-to-an-ontario-lake-for-17-years-lowering-ph-from-6-8-to-5-2-decades-later-its-lake-trout-population-remains-below-half-its-former-level/articleshow/133676293.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-01T15:25:22+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133676494,imgsize-825498.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Bird Numbers Rise On Ranch: Colorado couple’s adaptive grazing boosts species; detections double]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133675718.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Lance and Lisa Wheeler's Colorado ranch has transformed into a sanctuary for grassland birds, boasting a remarkable doubling in species detection since 2019. Their innovative farming methods, coupled with adaptive grazing strategies, promote rich habitats that support diverse wildlife. As evidenced by a 26% increase on the ranch's Bird-Friendliness Index, this holistic approach successfully merges livestock management with conservation efforts.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2014-a-colorado-couple-bought-land-to-build-a-family-ranch-by-2025-bird-species-had-risen-from-29-to-37-and-grassland-bird-detections-doubled-from-178-to-356/articleshow/133675718.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-2014-a-colorado-couple-bought-land-to-build-a-family-ranch-by-2025-bird-species-had-risen-from-29-to-37-and-grassland-bird-detections-doubled-from-178-to-356/articleshow/133675718.cms]]></guid><